<resheader name="resmimetype"><value>text/microsoft-resx</value></resheader><resheader name="version"><value>1.3</value></resheader><resheader name="reader"><value>System.Resources.ResXResourceReader, System.Windows.Forms, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089</value></resheader><resheader name="writer"><value>System.Resources.ResXResourceWriter, System.Windows.Forms, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089</value></resheader><data name="labelTS1.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>This can be used to add a radio that is not responding
to a discovery request. Some Protocol 1 firmwares require
the UDP discovery packet to be sent to 255.255.255.255
and if this radio is behind a router with fowarded ports
for example (without vpn etc) then it will not respond.

No details will be known about the radio, so:
- the protocol detection will not operate so you
   will need to set it correctly
- the hardware board ID will be taken from the model
   currently selected in setup
- the firmware version will not be unknown
- the radio mac address will show 'Custom' instead
- the details will not be updated if a connection is made
   and anything is different to the settings here</value></data>
